title: Implement the serial autorecovery monitor and rate-limited queue
updated_at: "2026-10-17T08:04:24Z"
---
Implement a T3-owned periodic monitor with approximately 60s cadence, one global serial worker, at least 1000ms between dispatches, bounded queue behavior, cancellation on shutdown, and per-failure dedupe so one observed failure cannot produce repeated Continue messages every scan.

Implementation note: the worker must re-read binding and projection state immediately before each dispatch; a scan snapshot is advisory only. Treat missing/archived/deleted/rebound threads as per-candidate skips. A failed dispatch must not poison later candidates, and durable command receipts must prevent duplicate accepted commands while preserving a clear policy for rejected attempts. Keep the limiter one worker/source per T3 process; do not imply host-wide coordination.

Implementation landed in sibling T3 Code checkout /home/xertrov/src/t3code on feat/c2c-autorecover and was fast-forwarded to local main. Core commits: 034cf7dd, 90e1e48d, 748e9389, 1fe4af4a, 89735b5a. The worker uses a 60s due gate, process-wide serial 1s spacing, deterministic ordering, 256-candidate cap, and retryable preflight/stale guard failures. Independent review passed after the no-receipt stale path was added.